SwiftPutty local patch 0003
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   reported upstream (2026-10-19); suitable for upstreaming

unix/network.c: free the error message of a failed asynchronous connect.

When a non-blocking connect() fails, net_select_result() builds the
error text with dupstr()/dupprintf() and passes it to plug_log(), which
only formats it into an Event Log line. The string was never freed, so
every failed connection attempt (each candidate address tried) leaked
it. Found by `leaks --atExit` on SwiftPutty's session tests.

--- a/unix/network.c
+++ b/unix/network.c
@@ -1427,6 +1427,7 @@
                     thisaddr = sk_extractaddr_tmp(s->addr, &s->step);
                     plug_log(s->plug, &s->sock, PLUGLOG_CONNECT_FAILED,
                              &thisaddr, s->port, errmsg, err);
+                    sfree(errmsg);
 
                     while (err && s->addr && sk_nextaddr(s->addr, &s->step)) {
                         err = try_connect(s);
